{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact fbec2ce9ba5b5d695e509f0dee219886f659fe56 under review a3550ce5 and promise3f4b81e9, governing assigned implementation request da2018c9 (#20112) and promise464731c7. Reporting artifact88b57411 is first; all eight exact-path candidates are included. I rechecked the current conditions, actual reporting chain and ordinary inherited staleness: all eight remain live and none describes_superseded_world. The prior changes-requested verdict725ba9a9 was ratified by904ecbc3; the corrected artifacts explicitly cite it and Planner finding9e7cca3f.\n\nAll three findings are resolved. [The command](cmd/gitseq-github/main.go@fbec2ce9ba5b5d695e509f0dee219886f659fe56:106) resolves routing only after the proposal branch and before loading the observation signing key. The real authorized dry-run proposal now succeeds under a malformed advertisement. [The new end-to-end test](cmd/gitseq-github/routing_test.go@fbec2ce9ba5b5d695e509f0dee219886f659fe56:308) uses a chartered clause, controlled tracker and real loopback resident; it proves the production observation crosses that socket, while the local sentinel does not dial it. The [submit comment](cmd/gitseq-github/main.go@fbec2ce9ba5b5d695e509f0dee219886f659fe56:539) now limits definite non-delivery to refused dial and describes an ambiguous lost reply without claiming an unchanged log.\n\nI independently ran five actual source omissions in a separate checkout: passing the raw flag at the production append call while retaining route validation, moving the route gate before the proposal branch, removing production route resolution, removing RefusedDial, and falling back locally on resident failure. Every mutant fails its behavioral control; none is a compilation failure. The original advertised/default/explicit/sentinel/refusal matrix and unchanged-head/depth controls pass.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers5 and7 are the application advertisement contract and CLI/connector routing. internal/residentclient owns one shared ResolveServerURL/RefusedDial implementation extracted from gs; cmd/gs and cmd/gitseq-github use it. The same-head [architecture page](docs/reference/architecture.md@fbec2ce9ba5b5d695e509f0dee219886f659fe56:387), candidatee04abacc, records the contract. All descriptive document candidates rest on current behavior producers. cmd/gitseq-mcp is unchanged.\n\nSecurity: the observation route is validated before connector custody is read or a request is built; malformed, foreign and non-loopback advertisements refuse. Resident unreachability and HTTP refusal never trigger local fallback. Signature/charter/admission identity and idempotency behavior, gs authority-command refusal and explicit local override, exact-frontier verification, loopback/redirect/response bounds and cancellation are preserved. The new tracker seam is package-private, restored by test cleanup and adds no runtime input or authority surface. No unresolved security defect was found. This is assigned work under the existing adopted routing outcome, not self-initiated work using an authority-bearing-request shortcut.\n\nSimplification: retain the one resolver and the one client-construction seam. Observation-only dispatch and narrower delivery wording remove the prior unnecessary coupling and false assurance. No additional cache, authority API or duplicate policy is needed.\n\nValidation at this exact head: uncached connector18.486s, residentclient0.545s, internal/app70.680s, gs resolver/authority/transport/frontier controls33.315s and docset57.591s pass; targeted vet and git diff --check pass. All eight API previews are byte-exact to Git. The only delta from previously reviewed5a0fbc38 is the two connector files; the author's whole-repository pass is at5a0fbc38, not an independently rerun whole-fbec suite. No live GitHub, key/custody, resident renewal or deployment operation was part of this review.\n\nClaude should ratify this exact approval, then seal the approved head with complete